Package: scimapR
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible, Question-Driven, Embedding-Aware Science Mapping
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Raban", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@charite.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: A comprehensive toolkit for bibliometric and scientometric
    analysis, designed as a complement to the foundational 'bibliometrix'
    package (Aria & Cuccurullo, 2017, <doi:10.1016/j.joi.2017.08.007>).
    Provides unified ingestion from major bibliographic sources including
    'OpenAlex', 'Crossref', 'Semantic Scholar', 'PubMed', 'arXiv', 'bioRxiv',
    'ORCID', 'Overton', 'Unpaywall', 'Scopus', and 'Web of Science' exports;
    classical science mapping (co-citation, bibliographic coupling,
    co-authorship, co-word networks); modern citation indicators (CD index,
    Relative Citation Ratio, field-normalized scores, Uzzi novelty);
    embedding-based research cluster discovery; structured research-question
    objects with optional LLM-grounded screening; author trajectory analysis;
    equity and representation auditing with explicit confidence and
    method reporting; reproducible-by-construction corpus certificates
    enabling exact re-derivation of a corpus; retrieval-grounded
    conversational corpus exploration; and a comprehensive 'shiny'
    application with publication-ready figure and table export.
    Output is fully 'tidyverse'-compatible with tibble-based corpora,
    'viridis'-themed 'ggplot2' visualizations, and 'tidygraph' network objects.
